# A friend's link /p/<code> shows p.html with a 200, keeping /p/<code> in the address bar
# (ADR 0008, ADR 0027). The target is /p, not /p.html: Cloudflare Pages answers /p.html
# with a 308 to /p, which would drop the code.
/p/*  /p  200
# A profile link /u/<username> shows u.html the same way (ADR 0020).
/u/*  /u  200
